# Regression test for kexhq/kex#379: `Template.scan` (which `Kex.embed` +
# `Template.text` run at compile time) was severely super-linear, so a
# template of ordinary real-world size — a few KB of HTML and CSS, nothing
# exotic — reliably blew through the scanner's hardcoded 2000ms budget and
# failed to compile at all. `large_template.ket` is ~9KB, well past every
# size that timed out in the issue; if the scanner regresses back to
# quadratic, this spec times out (via `make spec`'s own per-spec timeout)
# rather than printing the line below.
main do
  let greet = Template.text(Kex.embed("lib/compiled/large_template.ket"))
  IO.printLine(greet("world"))
end
